// Silent sound carrier: the sustained roar of a flamethrower. See
// snd_reload.json5 for why a trigger hook needs a particle to reach a sound
// at all, and for every "invisible and yet not fx-demoted" property this def
// inherits from it unchanged.
//
// THE ONE THING THAT IS DIFFERENT HERE: `cooldown`. The three flamers have
// `fire_delay: 1`, so `on.fire` runs SIXTY TIMES A SECOND, and a 0.32 s roar
// spawned sixty times a second is ~19 coherent copies of itself stacked on
// top of each other — a wall of noise that the master limiter would then pump
// on and off. The `sound` verb's `cooldown:` (ticks) is the re-trigger floor
// that fixes it: the carrier still spawns every tick, and the renderer drops
// every request that arrives inside 18 ticks of the last one from the same
// place. Same mechanism gus2wn gives a Gusanos continuous `detect_range`.
//
// So the cadence is 18 ticks = 0.300 s against a 0.320 s cell: the cell's
// 30 ms tail fade crossfades into the next cell's 20 ms head, and the roar is
// continuous for exactly as long as the trigger is down and not one tick
// longer. tools/cut-zk-flamer-sounds.sh cut the file to those numbers — the
// three of them (cell length, cooldown, fades) only work together.
//
// WHY NOT `on.open_fire`, which fires once per burst and needs no cooldown:
// because a full M9A1-7 magazine is 155 ticks of continuous flame and the cell
// is 19, so a burst-start sound would cover an eighth of it and leave the
// rest silent. WHY NOT a periodic `on.tick` carrier: `every:` is phased on the
// global frame counter, so it would work, but nothing would ever tell the
// carrier the trigger had come up. `on.fire` IS the "still firing" signal.
//
// The cooldown key is the verb id plus a 16 px cell of the sound's position,
// so two worms flaming at opposite ends of the map each get their own roar,
// and two worms flaming shoulder to shoulder share one. Both are right.
{
  "legacy": {
    "wallhack_bounce": -1
  },
  "physics": {
    "gravity": 0,
    "damping": 1,
    "wobble": 0,
    "pushed_by_blasts": false,
    "ccd": false,
    "substeps": 1
  },
  "radius": 0,
  "collide": {
    "terrain": false,
    "worms": false,
    "projectiles": false
  },
  "fuse": {
    "ticks": 2,
    "variance": 0
  },
  "on": {
    "fuse": [
      {
        "sound": {
          "file": "flamer_loop.ogg",
          "cooldown": 18
        }
      },
      {
        "remove": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "speed": 0
}
